  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC Middle East Humanitarian Crisis Appeal - Gaza (Phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the successful implementation of Phase 1 (PAL075), which provided life-saving support through multipurpose cash assistance (MPCA), primary healthcare, and mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS), this second phase of the response continues to address the urgent and growing needs of communities in Gaza.

With a continued focus on MPCA, Phase 2 aims to support vulnerable households to meet their immediate and basic needs amid ongoing instability. The project will also maintain access to essential healthcare services, delivered through a primary site in Deir al Balah, ensuring continuity of care for displaced and affected populations.

This second phase is being launched in a highly challenging operational context. After a brief ceasefire in January 2025, hostilities resumed in mid-March, accompanied by a full blockade on humanitarian aid from early March, which remains in place as of April 2025. These renewed restrictions and violence have deepened humanitarian needs and made access to basic services even more critical.</narrative>
  </description>
